  "notes": "West leads the ♣J against 3NT. West wins the first 4 tricks in clubs. West switches to a diamond, won in the closed hand. If diamonds are not breaking, South will need some sort of squeeze.\n\nEast must have the ♠Q as West would have opened the bidding with the ♠Q in addition to the 10 points in clubs and the ♦J he has already shown. If East has the diamond length, he can be squeezed if he has the ♠Q, ♠10, and ♠9 or 5 or more spades.\n\nIf West has the diamond length, he can be squeezed if he has the ♠10 and ♠9. In any case, South cashes the remaining top diamonds and runs the hearts. As West has the long diamonds as well as the required spade holding, he will have no good answer on the last heart. A diamond discard will make North's diamond good.\n\nA spade discard will allow South to take 3 spade tricks. The ♠J is led from North (the hand would have played equally well if the ♠J was led earlier). East must cover. South wins and his third spade will be worth a trick.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♣J against 3NT. West wins the first 4 tricks in clubs. West switches to a diamond, won in the closed hand. If diamonds are not breaking, South will need some sort of squeeze.",
    "East must have the ♠Q as West would have opened the bidding with the ♠Q in addition to the 10 points in clubs and the ♦J he has already shown. If East has the diamond length, he can be squeezed if he has the ♠Q, ♠10, and ♠9 or 5 or more spades.",
    "If West has the diamond length, he can be squeezed if he has the ♠10 and ♠9. In any case, South cashes the remaining top diamonds and runs the hearts. As West has the long diamonds as well as the required spade holding, he will have no good answer on the last heart. A diamond discard will make North's diamond good.",
    "A spade discard will allow South to take 3 spade tricks. The ♠J is led from North (the hand would have played equally well if the ♠J was led earlier). East must cover. South wins and his third spade will be worth a trick."
